     1,
     "<p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">Subject:\r\nAnnouncing the NEW AND IMPROVED Konfound-it app and upcoming workshops</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">We have\r\nreleased a new versions of the konfound package in R (1.0.2) and in\r\nStata. Features include:</p><ul style=\"margin-top:0in\" type=\"disc\">\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Conditional Robustness of Inference for\r\n     Replacement (CRIR)</b> in which there is no relationship between predictor\r\n     and outcome in the replacement data <i>conditional </i>on other terms in\r\n     the model (e.g., for use with interaction effects when models include main\r\n     effects as applied in diff in diff).</li>\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>2x2 and logistic regression added to Stata</b>\r\n     (already in R).  <ul style=\"margin-top:0in\" type=\"circle\">\r\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">More options for Fragility index\r\n      (e.g., <i>switch_trm</i>)</li>\r\n </ul></li>\r\n \r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Unconditional Impact Threshold for a Confounding\r\n     Variable</b> is provided when possible.<ul style=\"margin-top:0in\" type=\"circle\">\r\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"> See Lonati, S., &amp; Wulff,\r\n      J. N. (2024). <a href=\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/pdf/10.1177/01492063241293126\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/pdf/10.1177/01492063241293126&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3gjCxih14f3cj4ijsuxAgr\">Hic\r\n      Sunt Dracones: On the risks of comparing the ITCV with control variable\r\n      correlations</a>. <i>Journal of Management</i>.</li>\r\n </ul></li>\r\n \r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b><a href=\"https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/s63onxsg6yoga5of9nd42/Quantifying-Sensitivity-to-Selection-on-Unobserved-Covariates-2024-distribute.pdf?rlkey=4yyxd9p3ej605n77vrbqq6pq3&amp;dl=0__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zpMSsYu7$\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/s63onxsg6yoga5of9nd42/Quantifying-Sensitivity-to-Selection-on-Unobserved-Covariates-2024-distribute.pdf?rlkey%3D4yyxd9p3ej605n77vrbqq6pq3%26dl%3D0__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zpMSsYu7$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rJQi61NMF8VAavn5YegYA\">Coefficient\r\n     of Proportionality</a></b> – how strong would selection on unobserved\r\n     covariates have to be relative to observed covariates to nullify an\r\n     estimated effect. <i>index = &quot;COP&quot;</i></li>\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Directly specify a threshold for inference</b>\r\n     (other than statistical significance) via <i>eff_thr</i></li>\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Specify a non-zero null hypothesis</b> for\r\n     significance testing via <i>nu</i></li>\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Application to What Works Clearinghouse <a href=\"https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-project.shinyapps.io/wwc-sensitivity-benchmark/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zsKKqHXZ$\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-project.shinyapps.io/wwc-sensitivity-benchmark/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zsKKqHXZ$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00RYdkJBRfvizvdpEmgRMP\">Benchmarks</a></b>\r\n     for educational research</li>\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">All raw results provided (in R, <i>to_return =\r\n     &quot;raw&quot;</i>, in Stata use <i>“return list”</i> after command)</li>\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">Improved statements in print out </li>\r\n <li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">Improved <a href=\"https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-project.shinyapps.io/konfound-it/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zon_qC4m$\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-project.shinyapps.io/konfound-it/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zon_qC4m$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2SE6OGt0fq_awrEOgGW7GQ\">konfound-it\r\n     app</a> interface: <a href=\"https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-project.shinyapps.io/konfound-it/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zon_qC4m$\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-project.shinyapps.io/konfound-it/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8zon_qC4m$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2SE6OGt0fq_awrEOgGW7GQ\">https://konfound-project.shinyapps.io/konfound-it/</a></li>\r\n</ul><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0in 0.5in;line-height:normal\"> </p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">Check out the <a href=\"https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-it.org/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8ziciNtK3$\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-it.org/__;!!IKRxdwAv5BmarQ!ZSV1LY6Cs1ARrgwXmanKjztYtZwUFof-PJDXZ_dzuLQvUYuvsvaPTGKVPC58iOD5lhQyWelhr4W4njj8ziciNtK3$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ep9rQIrWOWrJVyapZzdvW\">konfound-it\r\nweb site</a> for more. And be sure to check out the <b><a href=\"https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/77e5efc8-37b7-4813-9101-84898b31a227/audio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/77e5efc8-37b7-4813-9101-84898b31a227/audio&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1pw65ru_z4ePz3QxLXjtO1\">Podcast</a>!</b></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"> </p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Commands</b></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b><i>In R:</i></b></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">install.packages(&quot;konfound&quot;)</p>library(konfound)<br>pkonfound(est_eff = -9.01, std_err = .68, n_obs = 7639, n_covariates = 221)<br><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b><i>In Stata:</i></b></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">.   ssc\r\ninstall konfound<br>\r\n.   ssc install indeplist<br>\r\n.   ssc install moss<br>\r\n.   ssc install matsort</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">.  \r\npkonfound -9.01 .68 7639 221</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Upcoming workshops:</b></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><a href=\"https://statisticalhorizons.com/seminars/sensitivity-analysis-causal-inference/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://statisticalhorizons.com/seminars/sensitivity-analysis-causal-inference/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3zgxyaTYKSkfUkj1SRIACZ\">March\r\n5 and 6 for Statistical Horizons</a></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">April 1 (possibly\r\nApril 8) at 12:40-3:30 on my zoom: <a href=\"https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-wfnSFxhSoQcshwf6eEdW\">https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435</a>.  This will be a class meeting, but you can drop\r\nin.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">April 7 and 9 (10:10am-11:20)\r\non my zoom: <a href=\"https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-wfnSFxhSoQcshwf6eEdW\">https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435</a>.  This will be a class meeting, but you can drop\r\nin</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">Look for an\r\nannouncement re: <a href=\"https://www.icpsr.umich.edu/web/pages/sumprog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.icpsr.umich.edu/web/pages/sumprog/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3cpTjj72EvDUy4tq6XRQWb\">ICPSR</a>\r\nthis summer.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Sensitivity\r\nanalysis within a pragmatic world view</b></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0in 0.5in;line-height:normal\">Frank, K.A., Lin, Q.,\r\nMaroulis, S.J. (accepted). “<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/35lsbqmj95g8jhgymfg5w/Embracing-Essential-Discourse-in-Educational-Policy-about-Causal-Inferences-from-Observational-Studies-final-changes-accepted.pdf?rlkey=5tdibg7k7lw57zf2x53loli9q&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/35lsbqmj95g8jhgymfg5w/Embracing-Essential-Discourse-in-Educational-Policy-about-Causal-Inferences-from-Observational-Studies-final-changes-accepted.pdf?rlkey%3D5tdibg7k7lw57zf2x53loli9q%26dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3d5AGc9rsnfkSTMHt5XFgY\">Causal\r\nInferences from Observational Studies in Education Policy: Towards Pragmatic\r\nSocial Science</a>” <i>Handbook on Education Policy Research</i>. Published by\r\nthe American Educational Research Association. Lora Cohen-Vogel, Janelle Scott\r\nand Peter Youngs editors.</p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0in 0.5in;line-height:normal\"><a rel=\"nofollow\"><span lang=\"FR\"> </span></a></p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0in 0.5in;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"FR\">Frank, K.A., Lin, Q.,\r\nXu, R., Maroulis, S.J., Mueller, A. (2023). </span><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/4vvpvgqhpe2h1rv/Quantifying%20the%20robustness%20of%20causal%20inferences%20as%20published%20sensitivity%20analysis%20for%20pragmatic%20social%20science.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/4vvpvgqhpe2h1rv/Quantifying%2520the%2520robustness%2520of%2520causal%2520inferences%2520as%2520published%2520sensitivity%2520analysis%2520for%2520pragmatic%2520social%2520science.pdf?dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244426344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2oP6LXsMkCjE_RyOMmgDeg\">Quantifying the Robustness of Causal\r\nInferences: Sensitivity Analysis for Pragmatic Social Science</a>.  <i>Social\r\nScience Research.</i> <i>110, 102815. </i>ERIC:<span style=\"color:black\">ED628601.</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><b>Support:</b></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\">Thanks to U.S.\r\nDepartment of Education Institute for Education Sciences through R305D220022 to\r\nMichigan State University. The opinions expressed are those of the authors and\r\ndo not represent views of the Institute for education Sciences or the U.S.\r\nDepartment. of Education.</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"> </p>"
